ion uses \"I\", \"my\" which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n    92→  - Confidence: HIGH (fundamental NER limitation, requires different approach to fix)\n    93→\n    94→**Changes Made:**\n    95→- File: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/validator.py`\n    96→- Line 165-178: **Removed** overly aggressive heuristic that auto-accepted high-mention-count names without LLM validation\n    97→- Line 39-54: **Enhanced** validation system prompt to explicitly reject objects, food, drink, places\n    98→- Line 66-69: **Enhanced** validation prompt template to ask LLM to distinguish between people and objects being discussed\n    99→\n   100→**Smoke Test Results (PASS):**\n   101→- Ran analysis on \"The Cask of Amontillado - Poe.txt\" with qwen2.5:32b\n   102→- ✅ \"Amontillado\" removed from character list (went from 3 to 2 characters)\n   103→- ✅ Narrator correctly identified as \"Montresor\" in plot summary\n   104→- ✅ Plot summary says \"The story is narrated by Montresor\" (not \"Amontillado\")\n   105→- ❌ Montresor still has only 1 mention (NER limitation - deferred as separate issue)\n   106→\n   107→**Full Test Suite: PASSED**\n   108→- 444 tests passed, 11 skipped, 1 warning\n   109→- No regressions introduced\n   110→\n   111→**Issues Addressed:**\n   112→- ✅ Issue #1: Fixed (Amontillado no longer extracted as character)\n   113→- ✅ Issue #2: Fixed (Montresor correctly identified as narrator in plot summary)\n   114→- ✅ Issue #5: Fixed (plot summary now uses \"Montresor\" not \"Amontillado\")\n   115→- ⏸️ Issue #3: Partially addressed (narrator identified but profile still thin due to 1 mention - NER limitation)\n   116→\n   117→## Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): NER extracting invalid character name \"--yes\"\n   118→\n   119→**Pipeline Failure:**\n   120→- Analysis failed during character extraction phase\n   121→- Error: `LLM validation returned invalid JSON for '--yes' after 3 attempts: Invalid JSON: got list`\n   122→\n   123→**Root Cause Analysis:**\n   124→- Location: Text line 166 of \"The Cask of Amontillado - Poe.txt\"\n   125→- Context: Fortunato's dialogue: \"He! he! he! --he! he! he! --yes, the Amontillado...\"\n   126→- spaCy NER tagged \"--yes\" as a PERSON entity (incorrect)\n   127→- The string \"--yes\" passed `_is_valid_name()` check (60% alphabetic ratio: 3 of 5 chars)\n   128→- Went to LLM validation, but LLM returned invalid JSON format (list instead of dict)\n   129→\n   130→**Why Previous Fix Didn't Address This:**\n   131→- Previous fix (Attempt 1) only removed the heuristic auto-acceptance\n   132→- Did not add filtering for names starting with punctuation\n   133→- spaCy occasionally mis-tags punctuation-heavy fragments as PERSON entities\n   134→\n   135→**Proposed Fix:**\n   136→- Add check in `_is_valid_name()` (src/pipeline/character_extraction/proposers/ner.py:237)\n   137→- Reject names that start or end with non-alphabetic characters\n   138→- Example: `if not name[0].isalpha() or not name[-1].isalpha(): return False`\n   139→\n   140→## Attempt 2 Analysis Run (2026-01-18): FAILED - NER bug still present\n   141→\n   142→**Error Encountered:**\n   143→```\n   144→LLM validation attempt 1 for '--yes' returned invalid JSON: got list\n   145→LLM validation attempt 2 for '--yes' returned invalid JSON: got list\n   146→LLM validation attempt 3 for '--yes' returned invalid JSON: got list\n   147→Validation failed for '--yes': LLM validation returned invalid JSON for '--yes' after 3 attempts: Invalid JSON: got list\n   148→Error during analysis: LLM validation returned invalid JSON for '--yes' after 3 attempts: Invalid JSON: got list\n   149→```\n   150→\n   151→**Analysis:**\n   152→- Confirmed the bug documented in Attempt 2 is still present\n   153→- NER is extracting \"--yes\" from text and sending it to LLM validation\n   154→- Current `_is_valid_name()` function (line 237-257) accepts \"--yes\" because:\n   155→  - It has 5 characters (passes `len(name) < 2` check on line 239)\n   156→  - It has 